# Every Dockerfile in this repo (apps/server, apps/worker, apps/web) is
# built with the REPO ROOT as its context (see each Dockerfile's own
# "IMPORTANT - build context" comment - pnpm workspaces need the root
# lockfile/config), so this file - not a per-app one - is what actually
# controls what `docker build`/`docker compose build` sends over. Mirrors
# .gitignore's list (regenerated-in-the-image build output, and anything
# that shouldn't leave a developer's machine) plus two Docker-specific
# entries .gitignore has no reason to carry: the Dockerfiles' own builder
# stage does `COPY . .` before `pnpm install`, and without this file that
# copy would also pull in a possibly-stale/wrong-platform node_modules
# (wasting build time and cache, and risking arch-mismatched native
# binaries) and - the real risk - .env's real secrets, baked into an
# image layer that could end up cached or pushed to a registry even
# though no runtime stage below ever COPYs .env out of the builder.

# Dependencies - regenerated by each Dockerfile's own `pnpm install`,
# never copied in from the host (wrong platform/arch risk otherwise).
node_modules

# Build output - regenerated inside the image by each Dockerfile's own
# build step; never trust build artifacts from the host.
dist
build
.turbo
.svelte-kit

# Env files - never bake real secrets into an image layer. Each service's
# actual runtime config comes from docker-compose.yml's `env_file: [.env]`
# on the running container, not from anything inside the image itself.
.env
.env.local
*.log

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store

# Test coverage
coverage

# Claude Code harness state (e.g. isolated worktrees for background agents) - never project source
.claude

# Git metadata - large, and no Dockerfile in this repo needs it (nothing
# here runs `git describe`/reads `.git` for a version string).
.git
